SUMMARY:Andy Warhol’s 'Screen Tests' + Conrad Ventur’s 'Screen Tests 
 Revisited'\, Pgm 2
LOCATION:Anthology Film Archives\, 32 Second Avenue\, Manhattan
DESCRIPTION:These two programs pair Warhol’s seminal and often exquisit
 e SCREEN TESTS – the silent\, black-and-white\, three-and-a-half minute
  filmic portraits he made between 1964-66\, which grew to encompass 472 s
 eparate reels\, portraying 189 individual subjects (many of them sitting 
 for multiple portraits) – with Conrad Ventur’s 21st-century remakes. 
 For Ventur’s (ongoing) project\, he has sought out as many… https://w
 ww.anthologyfilmarchives.org/film_screenings/calendar?view=list&month=11&
 year=2026#showing-62295
URL:https://www.anthologyfilmarchives.org/film_screenings/calendar?view=l
 ist&month=11&year=2026#showing-62295
